00:46:51.718 --> 00:46:54.196
And they're like, "We hate you."

1049
00:46:54.196 --> 00:46:55.396
And you're like, "What!"

1050
00:46:56.846 --> 00:47:00.530
But so all that to say, I didn't know.

1051
00:47:00.530 --> 00:47:04.700
I had this like passionate calling to be a writer

1052
00:47:04.700 --> 00:47:07.180
until I was close to 30.

1053
00:47:07.180 --> 00:47:08.840
I thought I was burned

1054
00:47:08.840 --> 00:47:11.920
by this idea because when I was a little kid

1055
00:47:11.920 --> 00:47:14.700
I saw "Jurassic Park" when I was 10 years old.

1056
00:47:14.700 --> 00:47:16.930
And I was like

1057
00:47:16.930 --> 00:47:19.230
this is the best movie that's ever been made.

1058
00:47:19.230 --> 00:47:22.450
And I am gonna dedicate my life to dinosaurs.

1059
00:47:22.450 --> 00:47:26.410
And then I realized I have to become Steven Spielberg.

1060
00:47:26.410 --> 00:47:28.557
I have to, I'm so obsessed.

1061
00:47:28.557 --> 00:47:32.150
That was my first like true idol.

1062
00:47:32.150 --> 00:47:33.480
And then I was obsessed

1063
00:47:33.480 --> 00:47:35.310
with all his movies and James Cameron

1064
00:47:35.310 --> 00:47:39.420
and George Lucas and that generation obsessed.

1065
00:47:39.420 --> 00:47:43.150
And I started telling people,

1066
00:47:43.150 --> 00:47:45.720
I'm going to become the next Steven Spielberg.

1067
00:47:45.720 --> 00:47:46.770
So buckle up.

1068
00:47:46.770 --> 00:47:50.360
And so all of middle school, high school

1069
00:47:50.360 --> 00:47:52.190
everyone knew this.

1070
00:47:52.190 --> 00:47:54.410
They were like, everyone was like,

1071
00:47:54.410 --> 00:47:56.010
Jed's gonna go off and make movies.

1072
00:47:56.010 --> 00:47:57.080
He's gonna move to Hollywood.

1073
00:47:57.080 --> 00:47:59.070
And I'm like, that's right, I am.

1074
00:47:59.070 --> 00:48:02.910
And to the degree where when I graduated high school

1075
00:48:02.910 --> 00:48:05.083
teachers asked for my autograph.

1076
00:48:06.710 --> 00:48:10.230
Because they were like, wow, here he goes, he got into USE.

1077
00:48:10.230 --> 00:48:12.390
But you know, props for the conviction.

1078
00:48:12.390 --> 00:48:14.930
And I think it speaks to how powerful it is when you

1079
00:48:14.930 --> 00:48:17.470
when you kind of declare this is who I am

1080
00:48:17.470 --> 00:48:20.400
and the world kind of coalesces around that idea.

1081
00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:23.275
And they're like, yeah, I guess he's gonna be there.

1082
00:48:23.275 --> 00:48:24.300
Yes. I mean, there's also the,

1083
00:48:24.300 --> 00:48:25.820
there's also the tall poppy syndrome

1084
00:48:25.820 --> 00:48:27.810
where people wanna cut you down for having a big dream

1085
00:48:27.810 --> 00:48:30.390
but for whatever reason, I was encouraged.

1086
00:48:30.390 --> 00:48:32.410
So I moved to LA

1087
00:48:32.410 --> 00:48:35.340
and I go to my film classes and I realized--

1088
00:48:35.340 --> 00:48:38.253
You go to Spielberg's film school.

1089
00:48:39.131 --> 00:48:40.400
And you made that happen.

1090
00:48:40.400 --> 00:48:43.910
Yes. But it was all rooted in this idea

1091
00:48:43.910 --> 00:48:44.780
that I thought I knew

1092
00:48:44.780 --> 00:48:45.870
that I was supposed to do that.

1093
00:48:45.870 --> 00:48:48.090
And then I actually started doing it.

1094
00:48:48.090 --> 00:48:51.380
And I realized not only is this horrible

1095
00:48:51.380 --> 00:48:53.410
that I will be horrible at this.

1096
00:48:53.410 --> 00:48:54.310
And I hate this.

1097
00:48:54.310 --> 00:48:57.112
And I had this major in college

1098
00:48:57.112 --> 00:48:59.970
this major identity crisis of

1099
00:48:59.970 --> 00:49:02.280
I promised everyone I would do this thing

1100
00:49:03.320 --> 00:49:05.550
and now I'm doing it or trying to do it.

1101
00:49:05.550 --> 00:49:07.700
And now I don't wanna do it.

1102
00:49:07.700 --> 00:49:10.360
And so what do I do?

1103
00:49:10.360 --> 00:49:12.463
And I mean, ultimately I just had to give up

1104
00:49:12.463 --> 00:49:14.330
because I just knew I'd be terrible.

1105
00:49:14.330 --> 00:49:17.350
But then I was this rudderless boat

1106
00:49:17.350 --> 00:49:19.490
at my whole developing brain

1107
00:49:19.490 --> 00:49:22.940
in adolescents had had this very bright North

1108
00:49:22.940 --> 00:49:26.280
star that was just now wiped blank.

1109
00:49:26.280 --> 00:49:28.810
And so then I spent college undeclared

1110
00:49:28.810 --> 00:49:31.180
not knowing finally declaring English.

1111
00:49:31.180 --> 00:49:32.860
Then I went to law school because I was like,

1112
00:49:32.860 --> 00:49:34.880
well now I have no skills,

1113
00:49:34.880 --> 00:49:37.190
except I can know how to read a book.

1114
00:49:37.190 --> 00:49:39.240
So I'm gonna go to law school.

1115
00:49:39.240 --> 00:49:41.624
So I have like some tangible skill.

1116
00:49:41.624 --> 00:49:46.490
And then, I discover my friends have

1117
00:49:46.490 --> 00:49:48.120
started this nonprofit and they need a lawyer.

1118
00:49:48.120 --> 00:49:51.450
And I'm so like, exhausted from working

1119
00:49:51.450 --> 00:49:54.353
in the like legal jobs that I had in law school.

1120
00:49:54.353 --> 00:49:55.240
I was like, I just need to be

1121
00:49:55.240 --> 00:49:57.780
around a community of people doing something inspiring.

1122
00:49:57.780 --> 00:50:00.720
So what it was I was just kind of walking through

1123
00:50:00.720 --> 00:50:04.890
any door that was opened that felt right at the moment.

1124
00:50:04.890 --> 00:50:09.890
And I did not have this big eye from 19 to 27

1125
00:50:11.970 --> 00:50:14.330
I would have said, I don't know why I'm on this planet.

1126
00:50:14.330 --> 00:50:15.363
I have no idea.

1127
00:50:16.710 --> 00:50:21.710
And then it was really the slow,

1128
00:50:21.920 --> 00:50:23.070
what loves you?

1129
00:50:23.070 --> 00:50:25.620
Or no, what do you love and what loves you back?

1130
00:50:25.620 --> 00:50:27.810
This idea that I started Invisible Children

1131
00:50:27.810 --> 00:50:30.890
writing a lot of the campaigns and then being encouraged

1132
00:50:30.890 --> 00:50:32.703
by them like, we liked the way you said that.

1133
00:50:32.703 --> 00:50:34.920
Will you come into this meeting and help us write this.

1134
00:50:34.920 --> 00:50:36.500
I'm like, okay.

1135
00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:38.810
And then that float into them,

1136
00:50:38.810 --> 00:50:40.120
like we need you to be our head writer.

1137
00:50:40.120 --> 00:50:41.050
And I'm like, really?

1138
00:50:41.050 --> 00:50:42.800
They're like, we like the way you articulate.

1139
00:50:42.800 --> 00:50:46.790
And so, and I loved that so much.

1140
00:50:46.790 --> 00:50:48.090
It was sort of this ebb

1141
00:50:49.348 --> 00:50:50.181
and flow of actually paying attention

1142
00:50:50.181 --> 00:50:52.800
to the winds in the sails of my life

1143
00:50:52.800 --> 00:50:57.190
of where the wind is moving and like use that to go forward.

1144
00:50:57.190 --> 00:51:01.410
And so it was almost like uncovering the writer inside me.

1145
00:51:01.410 --> 00:51:04.763
And then once I started doing that and it bore fruit,

1146
00:51:07.200 --> 00:51:09.380
it made me feel very accomplished

1147
00:51:09.380 --> 00:51:13.290
and it made me feel very worthy to be alive.

1148
00:51:13.290 --> 00:51:18.290
And so if I really extrapolate what that means,

1149
00:51:19.750 --> 00:51:21.360
it's not like I think everyone has

1150
00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:22.920
some specific dream career.

1151
00:51:22.920 --> 00:51:27.920
I think everybody wants to do something that feels useful.

1152
00:51:29.430 --> 00:51:31.067
And I found that for myself.

1153
00:51:31.067 --> 00:51:33.160
But it's in the doing that you have

1154
00:51:33.160 --> 00:51:35.040
that discovery and the tacking,

1155
00:51:35.040 --> 00:51:36.740
like making little adjustments

1156
00:51:36.740 --> 00:51:38.050
along the way that are based

1157
00:51:38.050 --> 00:51:40.960
on external feedback that you're getting from others.

1158
00:51:40.960 --> 00:51:43.639
Like, Hey, you're pretty good at this.

1159
00:51:43.639 --> 00:51:45.300
And realizing, I actually like that.

1160
00:51:45.300 --> 00:51:46.760
And let me just maneuver

1161
00:51:46.760 --> 00:51:49.420
you know what I'm doing a little bit in this direction

1162
00:51:49.420 --> 00:51:52.080
until one day, you're like, I guess I'm a writer.

1163
00:51:52.080 --> 00:51:53.840
It kind of happened to you

1164
00:51:53.840 --> 00:51:56.280
in the process of you just moving forward

1165
00:51:56.280 --> 00:51:59.050
with your life as opposed to declaring in middle school.

1166
00:51:59.050 --> 00:52:00.740
Like I'm gonna be hacks before,

1167
00:52:00.740 --> 00:52:02.840
you know what that means.

1168
00:52:02.840 --> 00:52:03.700
But not for nothing.

1169
00:52:03.700 --> 00:52:06.630
I actually think you'd be a very good filmmaker

1170
00:52:06.630 --> 00:52:07.463
good director.

1171
00:52:09.080 --> 00:52:11.090
Maybe not like a "Jurassic Park"

1172
00:52:11.090 --> 00:52:13.210
like I see you more as like a Mike Nichols.

1173
00:52:13.210 --> 00:52:17.280
Like you're somebody who I am certain would work very well

1174
00:52:17.280 --> 00:52:19.860
with actors in an emotional setting

1175
00:52:19.860 --> 00:52:22.873
and could make like a wonderful movie like that.

1176
00:52:24.100 --> 00:52:26.133
I mean, God knows, I love the idea.

1177
00:52:27.670 --> 00:52:30.630
But back on this idea of you know

1178
00:52:30.630 --> 00:52:34.120
like the pressure to find your passion

1179
00:52:34.120 --> 00:52:37.373
or to have this career, that's gonna, you know,

1180
00:52:38.300 --> 00:52:42.030
be sort of big in the scheme of how culture

1181
00:52:42.030 --> 00:52:43.100
perceives these things.

1182
00:52:43.100 --> 00:52:46.340
You talk about your friendship with Tom.

1183
00:52:46.340 --> 00:52:48.590
And I can only assume this is Tom Shadyac.

1184
00:52:48.590 --> 00:52:49.423
It is right.

1185
00:52:49.423 --> 00:52:50.540
Of course it is.

1186
00:52:50.540 --> 00:52:52.500
It's like, this is definitely Tom Shadyac

1187
00:52:52.500 --> 00:52:55.980
and he has this great line where he tells you

1188
00:52:57.360 --> 00:53:00.410
your generation has an idolatry of magnitude.

1189
00:53:00.410 --> 00:53:01.880
And it's probably one

1190
00:53:01.880 --> 00:53:03.360
of my favorite lines in the whole book.

1191
00:53:03.360 --> 00:53:07.290
So let's spend a few minutes talking about what that means.

1192
00:53:07.290 --> 00:53:10.220
Well, he, I remember he originally said

1193
00:53:10.220 --> 00:53:12.542
that talking about Invisible Children.

1194
00:53:12.542 --> 00:53:16.300
And he was because we were at Invisible Children

1195
00:53:16.300 --> 00:53:18.440
not only were we trying to arrest Joseph Kony

1196
00:53:18.440 --> 00:53:21.700
and end the longest running war in Central East Africa

1197
00:53:21.700 --> 00:53:23.570
but we also wanted to change the world.

1198
00:53:23.570 --> 00:53:26.380
We wanted to bolster international human rights.

1199
00:53:26.380 --> 00:53:29.130
We wanted war crimes against children to be something

1200
00:53:29.130 --> 00:53:32.340
that everyone on the planet cares about and rallies around.

1201
00:53:32.340 --> 00:53:36.570
It was such this like giant thing

1202
00:53:36.570 --> 00:53:40.330
and pinning it all on arresting Joseph Kony.

1203
00:53:40.330 --> 00:53:43.850
And seeing him tried before the ICC was such this, like

1204
00:53:43.850 --> 00:53:45.940
if we haven't done that we have failed.

1205
00:53:45.940 --> 00:53:48.760
And he would always say, he's such a mentor in our life.

1206
00:53:48.760 --> 00:53:52.590
He's like, you have put thousands of kids through schools.

1207
00:53:52.590 --> 00:53:53.940
You have built schools

1208
00:53:53.940 --> 00:53:56.280
you have awakened hundreds of thousands

1209
00:53:56.280 --> 00:53:58.680
if not millions of Western teenagers

1210
00:53:58.680 --> 00:54:00.380
to international human rights,

1211
00:54:00.380 --> 00:54:02.470
to caring about something outside their building

1212
00:54:02.470 --> 00:54:04.030
and their small world

1213
00:54:04.900 --> 00:54:06.820
you have gotten bills passed

1214
00:54:06.820 --> 00:54:08.520
through the Obama administration to help

1215
00:54:08.520 --> 00:54:11.420
with the pursuit of these war criminals.

1216
00:54:11.420 --> 00:54:12.660
You've done it.

1217
00:54:12.660 --> 00:54:14.120
You've done so much.

1218
00:54:14.120 --> 00:54:16.610
And you can't see it because you've decided

1219
00:54:16.610 --> 00:54:18.940
if you do not turn the world upside down

1220
00:54:18.940 --> 00:54:20.610
and change it then you have failed.

1221
00:54:20.610 --> 00:54:24.180
And that robs you of

1222
00:54:24.180 --> 00:54:27.440
both the stamina provided by incremental success.

1223
00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:28.940
And also just the reality

1224
00:54:28.940 --> 00:54:31.550
of understanding that it's not everyone's duty to

1225
00:54:31.550 --> 00:54:34.780
change the world changing someone's life,

1226
00:54:34.780 --> 00:54:36.100
right in front of you

1227
00:54:36.100 --> 00:54:39.250
or one child's life or five children's lives

1228
00:54:39.250 --> 00:54:43.770
whatever is so cosmically significant.

1229
00:54:43.770 --> 00:54:46.750
And if you overlook that, then you damage and disrespect

1230
00:54:46.750 --> 00:54:49.890
the impact you've already had or are having.

1231
00:54:49.890 --> 00:54:54.890
And I think a lot of people, whether it's I talk

1232
00:54:55.460 --> 00:54:57.100
with my agent and my editor about this a lot

1233
00:54:57.100 --> 00:54:58.910
because I get asked by people,

1234
00:54:58.910 --> 00:55:00.260
how do I get published?

1235
00:55:00.260 --> 00:55:01.270
How do I get noticed?

1236
00:55:01.270 --> 00:55:03.130
How do I get an agent?

1237
00:55:03.130 --> 00:55:08.130
And the question is that my agent calls it

1238
00:55:10.280 --> 00:55:12.350
the hidden desire behind the question.

1239
00:55:12.350 --> 00:55:16.100
It's like, what is the spirit of your question?

1240
00:55:16.100 --> 00:55:18.680
Because is it actually

1241
00:55:18.680 --> 00:55:22.960
how do I get validated for my writing?

1242
00:55:22.960 --> 00:55:24.500
And I need validation.

1243
00:55:24.500 --> 00:55:26.940
He says, it's also the hidden desire

1244
00:55:26.940 --> 00:55:27.990
in the question when someone says

1245
00:55:27.990 --> 00:55:30.320
how do you handle the critics?

1246
00:55:30.320 --> 00:55:35.320
And that the hidden nature of that question is how do I

1247
00:55:36.550 --> 00:55:38.560
I really care what people think

1248
00:55:38.560 --> 00:55:41.955
about my products so much so that I'm so afraid

1249
00:55:41.955 --> 00:55:43.410
of putting it out there because

1250
00:55:43.410 --> 00:55:44.680
what if someone doesn't like it

1251
00:55:44.680 --> 00:55:47.253
and I need validation for my work.

1252
00:55:48.620 --> 00:55:50.020
And so there's just this like,

1253
00:55:50.020 --> 00:55:54.070
idea that if I'm not published and on a bookshelf

1254
00:55:54.070 --> 00:55:55.640
if I'm not this or that,

1255
00:55:55.640 --> 00:55:57.390
if I haven't achieved A, B, C, D

1256
00:55:57.390 --> 00:55:59.343
or any than, I'm not a real blank.

1257
00:56:00.210 --> 00:56:04.210
And I think in the journey of figuring

1258
00:56:04.210 --> 00:56:06.900
out what you're good at and what love, what you love

1259
00:56:06.900 --> 00:56:08.620
and what loves you and what you're supposed to be doing

1260
00:56:08.620 --> 00:56:12.740
and how you can be useful and helpful in this life is

1261
00:56:13.970 --> 00:56:16.800
is if you feel a pull towards something

1262
00:56:16.800 --> 00:56:21.040
no matter how big or small, then like in some way, try it.

1263
00:56:21.040 --> 00:56:22.650
And that was my entire intention

1264
00:56:22.650 --> 00:56:24.640
with writing "To Shake the Sleeping Self"

1265
00:56:24.640 --> 00:56:27.100
was I don't know if I can write a book

1266
00:56:27.100 --> 00:56:30.540
I actually might be bad and I might embarrass myself

1267
00:56:30.540 --> 00:56:35.540
but I'm willing to try and put it out there.

1268
00:56:35.860 --> 00:56:39.260
And I'm so happy to self publish because I just

1269
00:56:39.260 --> 00:56:41.260
wanna hold it in my hands and know I did a thing.

1270
00:56:41.260 --> 00:56:44.230
And then I can move on with my life and find some other job.

1271
00:56:44.230 --> 00:56:46.700
Or if the wind doesn't tack in that direction

1272
00:56:46.700 --> 00:56:47.620
I'll tack the other way.

1273
00:56:47.620 --> 00:56:48.910
Great. I can do that.

1274
00:56:48.910 --> 00:56:51.170
But the writing was a compulsion.

1275
00:56:51.170 --> 00:56:52.890
It was something that had to be birthed.

1276
00:56:52.890 --> 00:56:54.020
You had to express it.

1277
00:56:54.020 --> 00:56:56.640
There was a call to the doing of it.

1278
00:56:56.640 --> 00:56:59.370
It wasn't about, can I get an agent or a book deal.

1279
00:56:59.370 --> 00:57:02.140
It was about basically the process

1280
00:57:02.140 --> 00:57:07.140
of giving voice to this thing that was inside of you.

1281
00:57:07.560 --> 00:57:09.560
Totally the writing in and of itself

1282
00:57:09.560 --> 00:57:10.900
is the thing I wanted to do,

1283
00:57:10.900 --> 00:57:13.300
because I had learned

1284
00:57:13.300 --> 00:57:18.300
that when I would write something originally

1285
00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:21.600
I had a blog on Blogspot,

1286
00:57:21.600 --> 00:57:22.740
which then became Tumblr

1287
00:57:22.740 --> 00:57:24.900
and it was called "The Water is Black"

1288
00:57:24.900 --> 00:57:26.100
which I love that title,

1289
00:57:27.050 --> 00:57:30.340
which came from a poem about being gay and God hating me.

1290
00:57:30.340 --> 00:57:35.340
And so I would write my thoughts

1291
00:57:35.350 --> 00:57:38.800
about my like sexuality and Christianity on this blog

1292
00:57:38.800 --> 00:57:41.120
just because when something would really

1293
00:57:41.120 --> 00:57:43.030
bother me this happens to me now.

1294
00:57:43.030 --> 00:57:47.320
Like something will really eat up my mind,

1295
00:57:47.320 --> 00:57:50.880
but I can feel the war of ideas in my head.

1296
00:57:50.880 --> 00:57:53.120
And then it's like, I just need to go sit down and write

1297
00:57:53.120 --> 00:57:55.850
about this and do some research and figure out what I think.

1298
00:57:55.850 --> 00:57:58.680
So it's the writing that gives you clarity

1299
00:57:58.680 --> 00:58:02.780
on what you actually believe about a specific thing?

1300
00:58:02.780 --> 00:58:05.350
Well, I don't know if you go for a number of days

1301
00:58:05.350 --> 00:58:07.250
without working out your,

1302
00:58:07.250 --> 00:58:10.470
my body starts to like ache hurt.

1303
00:58:10.470 --> 00:58:13.010
It's like, I don't know if that's atrophy or just stiffness

1304
00:58:13.010 --> 00:58:15.050
